WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.302
-Thank you very much
for watching us, everybody.

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:04.637
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.305
I want to say hello and welcome
back to Kamal Gray,

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:07.340
ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.008
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.643
Great to see you, Kamal.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.112
Roots, did you miss --
Did you miss Kamal?

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.747
-No, no, not really.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:15.914
We'll dub it in later.

00:00:15.914 --> 00:00:17.984
We'll put it in post.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.920
Welcome to the show again,
everybody.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.755
Do you guys know this?
This is crazy.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.424
The Olympics were supposed to
start around this time.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:27.794
Isn't that bizarre?

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:32.432
Yeah, but now with the virus,
it's just President Trump on TV.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.901
So instead of watching
gymnastics and swimming,

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.469
we're watching
a guy bend over backwards

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.871
to stay above water.

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:42.042
Last night,
Trump held a 27-minute briefing

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.510
and basically
read the entire thing.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.846
Fun fact -- on his script,
all the words were in

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:50.749
a little bubble coming from
a cartoon elephant.

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:53.720
Trump kept it short
and stuck to the script.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.455
Unfortunately, he sounded like
a kid reading a book report

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:58.257
he got off of SparkNotes.

00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:03.896
[ As Trump ] "Gatsby" was great.
Some even say the greatest.

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.531
[ Normal voice ] But Trump
kicked things off with

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.200
something I didn't
expect to hear

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.101
five months into the pandemic.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:14.173
-We are in the process of
developing a strategy

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:16.543
that's going to be
very, very powerful.

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.311
-Trump said working on a
strategy isn't that hard.

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:20.513
He found one on his desk

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:25.217
from the CDC
marked "February 1st."

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.186
He's working on a strategy now?

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.622
That's like Ford's Theatre being
like, "Good news, everyone.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.090
We're beefing up security."

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.360
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.630
That's right --
he's working on a strategy now.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:43.769
He was like, "The key
to disaster response is...

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:46.606
timing."

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.806
Yeah, Trump said
he's in the process

00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:49.742
of developing a strategy.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.044
He sounds like every dad
that's asked,

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.679
"When are you going to build
me that tree house?"

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:55.615
"I'm working on a strategy.
Just let me get another beer.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.851
We'll talk about it tomorrow."

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.454
Meanwhile, after months of
sounding upbeat about the virus,

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.723
Trump seemed like
he was changing his tune.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.758
-It will probably,
unfortunately,

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.393
get worse before it gets better.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.695
-Where have I heard that before?
Oh, yeah.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:12.899
Dr. Fauci has said
it every day since March.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.036
That's reassuring, though.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.737
We've from
"make America great again"

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:21.974
to "It will get worse
before it gets better."

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:24.077
Asked when it will get worse,
Trump was like,

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:27.847
"Oh, when I force
all the schools to reopen."

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.982
Well, to prove how seriously
he's taking things,

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:32.218
the president decided to talk
about his own commitment

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.586
to wearing a mask.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:37.823
-If you can, use the mask.
When you can, use the mask.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:40.559
If you're close to each other,
if you're in a group,

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:42.494
I would put it on
when I'm in a group.

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:44.430
I have no problem
with the masks.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.799
-Yeah, Trump said
he's always supported masks.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:52.471
He was like, "I wore one
far back as 11 days ago.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:55.507
Oh, there was also
Halloween 1968.

00:02:55.507 --> 00:02:58.844
I was Bozo the Clown."

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:00.579
Once Trump finished
reading from his script,

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:03.916
he went off book,
which is always a mistake,

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:05.718
and took some questions.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.186
One reporter asked
for his thoughts on

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:10.589
Jeffrey Epstein's longtime
associate, Ghislaine Maxwell,

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:13.225
being imprisoned on
sex-trafficking charges.

00:03:13.225 --> 00:03:14.793
Let's hear how that went.

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:16.929
-I just wish her well, frankly.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.998
I've met her numerous times
over the years,

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.833
especially since I lived
in Palm Beach

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.235
and I guess they lived
in Palm Beach.

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:26.138
But I wish her well.

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:29.342
-Ugh...

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.110
-What?

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.680
I would do a spit take right now
if it wasn't so dangerous.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.849
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.519
Later on, Trump had everyone
sign a Hallmark sympathy card

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:43.222
that said...

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.891
They're always sold out
when I go to the store.

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:49.428
Right after he wished her well,
Trump's staff was like,

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:50.496
"Oh, yeah.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:53.066
This is why we stopped
doing these."

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.134
Moving on to sports,
over in Poland,

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:58.237
some motorcycle-racing fans came
up with a creative way

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.538
to watch their home team.

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:00.974
Take a look at this.

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:03.309
Yeah, they rented 21 cranes

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:07.413
so they could watch their
local team race.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:10.316
Although, when you're watching
from a crane,

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.852
it's kind of hard to leave
without the racers noticing.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.454
"I'm going to take off, guys."

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.489
[ Whirring ]

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.563
They tried to do the wave,

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.598
but it was
absolutely terrifying.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.867
"Aah! Okay."

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:31.036
And, finally, some quirky, fun
news that we could all use.

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.039
A man in Jamaica
won the lottery,

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.541
but look at how he decided
to collect his prize.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:38.477 line:0%
-A lottery winner in
Jamaica showed up in

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:40.980 line:0%
a Darth Vader costume

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.283 line:0%
to claim his check for
95 million Jamaican dollars.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:49.054 line:0%
That's about
650,000 American dollars.

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:50.356
-Ever since
he won all that money,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.158
a dozen people
have come up to him like,

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:56.696
"You are my father? Please?"

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:59.031
Meanwhile, his ex
was watching that like,

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.800
"Yeah, still no regrets."

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.435
You guys know I've been
trying to keep up with

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:05.337
the news at much as I can,
but when it comes to

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:07.473
news about the economy,
there's only one place

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.041
I'd turn to get the facts.

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:15.881
It's "Market Crunch."
♪♪

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:18.083
Welcome back to CNBC's
"Market Crunch."

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:19.384
I'm Hal Grud.

00:05:19.384 --> 00:05:21.120
This week's market
in a nutshell --

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.023
America wants to order a
Happy Meal with a toy in it

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.591
but just keeps getting a
Grumpy Meal

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.660
with a piece of black licorice
stuck to the bag.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.630
Let's break it down. Break it!

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.332
In commodities,
we're seeing widespread reports

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:36.902
of couples getting married --
for the rice.

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:40.173
Here comes the "no, thank you"!

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.442
Crude oil continues to
plunge this week,

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:44.910
forcing people
to sell their cars --

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.512
for gas money!

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.914
Not pumped!

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:50.182
Let's look at gold.

00:05:50.182 --> 00:05:53.752
Today, 2 Chainz is now just
1 Chain -- singular.

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:56.622
That's not enough chains.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.492
In international trade,
a fake Nigerian prince

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:02.494
I met online tried to
wire money to me.

00:06:02.494 --> 00:06:05.130
Reverse scam.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.699
Let's look at the closing bell.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:09.768
What?! No bell?
They had to sell it?

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:11.637
Clang, clang, gone!

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.806
And now, time for
my "Market Perspective."

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.209 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:17.676
This is usually
the part of the show

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:19.779
where I offer my expert opinion
on the market,

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:22.648
but these days, I can't even
put in my two cents.

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:24.516
No cents!

00:06:24.516 --> 00:06:26.552
Up next, the pot.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:29.521
Will we have one to piss in?
No piss pot?!

00:06:29.521 --> 00:06:32.992
Also, the Dow.
More like Down.

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:35.461
This has been "Market Crunch."

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.629
♪♪

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.898
-"Market Crunch."

